Initial git status showed no unexpected output outside the task scope.

=== SURVEY ===
Read cmd\teslasync\main.go, internal\api\telemetry_handler.go, internal\signal\live_store.go, internal\signal\store.go, internal\signal\redis_cache.go, internal\signal\live_store_test.go, internal\config\config.go, docker-compose.yml, helm\teslasync\values.yaml, and helm\teslasync\templates\configmap.yaml.
Found telemetry ingestion updating signal.Store and Redis separately.
Found startup calling signalStore.LoadFromDB before signal_history hydration.
Found LiveSignalStore boundary with hybrid/local modes and Redis-first Warm support.

=== REASONING ===
Telemetry ingestion must keep local L1 writes synchronous for FSM/session/snapshot merge while avoiding duplicate direct Redis writes in telemetry_handler.go.
The live-store boundary now provides a non-blocking telemetry update path that performs L1 synchronously and mirrors Redis asynchronously with a bounded timeout.
Startup should construct the live store from the local Store plus optional Redis cache, warm Redis before history, and leave FSM/session/alert hot paths on local SignalStore.
LIVE_SIGNAL_STORE_MODE is non-secret configuration, so it was added to config binding, Docker Compose, Helm values, and Helm configmap.

=== CHANGES ===
Added TelemetryHandler.liveSignalStore plus SetLiveSignalStore and routed ProcessSignals live-state writes through LiveSignalStore.UpdateNonBlocking once per batch.
Kept signalStore for local-hot-path consumers and snapshot merge context.
Kept redisCache in TelemetryHandler for SSE Pub/Sub and startup cache forwarding only; removed direct Redis HSET updates from telemetry_handler.go.
Added LiveSignalStore.UpdateNonBlocking with synchronous L1 update and bounded asynchronous Redis mirror.
Adjusted Redis warmup to skip timestamp-less legacy values so signal_history Hydrate can fill missing or unknown-freshness keys.
Constructed and wired the live store in cmd\teslasync\main.go with Redis-first Warm followed by bounded signal_history Hydrate.
Added LIVE_SIGNAL_STORE_MODE=hybrid|local config wiring across internal config, docker-compose, and Helm.
Added unit tests for L1-only telemetry writes, live-store call count, Redis failure preserving L1, non-blocking L2 attempts, local mode, and Redis-before-history warmup behavior.
